WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
VIEWS OF THE PEAK

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.190
No...

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.320
Are you two... the crushers?

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.200
Crushers?

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.530
What...

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.450
are you going to do?

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.950
Hey!

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.330
What did Yokota tell you?

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.080
He suddenly came out with
talk of going to Bali.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.540
He was acting really weird.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.920
What did you bastards do to him?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.970
There's nothing to worry about.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.390
Huh?

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.680
You must be getting weary of
all those troubling thoughts.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.730
I'm sure you'd like to rest a while.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:30.850
Why don't you rest

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.320
and forget about everything that
happened today?

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.700
Dammit.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.830
That jerk-off Katsuragi flapping his lips,
calling us "crushers".

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.750
I guess it must be a generational thing.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.830
Back in the day,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.790
people like us were called "crushers".

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.170
We'd wreak havoc in those loci
you call "peaks" and "valleys",

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.960
and that would be it for the target.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.260
Right...

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.220
Since you lot came on the scene
with your "images",

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.760
the requests from the guys upstairs
have got more and more demanding.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.480
I mean, what do they expect
from me, miracles? Seriously...

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.980
I had to hypnotize Kenji and Yokota
on my own that day.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.690
I'm sure it isn't easy
for you, Mr. Katsuragi.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.030
Having an image makes things easier and
you can avoid getting trapped in valleys.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:24.830
-What?
-Err... Nothing.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.790
Ah, I guess they're done.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.040
What's all this?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.000
That's the trigger we used.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:40.970
We planted a thought in his mind that
we knew would set him off when he read it.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.010
Yokota hadn't told him anything, man.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.930
So, he really did just forget
to leave that key...

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.350
How about we send Kenji
to some island in the Pacific?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.270
Then we can run this place ourselves.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.780
You'll need to crush him, Hiroki.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.570
What the hell for?
We erased his memory of last night!

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.820
What do we need to crush him for?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.200
When Yokota's body gets identified,
the cops will come looking for Kenji!

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.330
We need to get him out of the picture
before that happens.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.710
You mean "kill him".

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.340
Right. Since he's Yokota's accomplice.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.970
Why else get them to swap cars
in full view of the street cameras?

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.800
We could just manipulate
his memories, though!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.180
It's too late for all that.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:34.020
It'll be in the paper tomorrow that Yokota
killed someone then committed suicide.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.480
What would Kenji think if he saw that?

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.110
Letting him live will cause
nothing but headaches.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.030
Headaches?

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.200
The one who's caused all
the headaches around here

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.490
is you, Katsuragi.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.160
Hiroki! Stop!

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.250
Mr. Katsuragi! Mr. Katsuragi!

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.000
Mr. Katsuragi!

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.260
Come back!

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.590
You want to cut a deal?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.100
Is Kenji really that important to you?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:14.600
After all we've done for you.(Shit! He's trapped me in my own memory!)

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.730
What are you doing?

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:22.280
Mr. Katsuragi, you need to stop this!

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.150
Tell me where the counterfeit bills
you stole are.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.740
Crap! Satoru!

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.500
I've screwed this up, Satoru!

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.580
Get me out of here, now!

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.010
Mr. Katsuragi!

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.840
Shit. He's stuck in Yokota's valley.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:53.060
I told you not to make threats
and synchronize at the same time!

00:05:58.810 --> 00:05:59.860
Mr. Katsuragi!

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:08.410
Yokota's memories of when his little
brother was killed are all here.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.450
This is his valley.
There's no doubt about it.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.120
If that's the case,
make sure you don't crush him.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.080
There's still a bunch of
questions I have to ask him.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.590
It's already too late.
If Yokota now sees you as his brother,

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.090
his memories no longer make any sense!
You've destroyed his valley!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.550
Feet?

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:43.770
Yokota's been crushed, you realize?

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.440
This is gonna cause a headache.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:46.900
Mr. Katsuragi!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.620
Are you all right, Mr. Katsuragi?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:01.540
Sorry about that.
You pissed me off, though.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:05.170
I'll show you who's pissed off,
you pinhead!

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:09.380
Anyway, we've got no choice.
Kenji's gotta be crushed!

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:14.510
There might be another way.
One that doesn't involve crushing him.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.390
Ultimately, we want Kenji
not to find it suspect that

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.350
Yokota became a murderer and
then committed suicide.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.360
So, all we need to do is transform
his memories of Yokota

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:28.900
so that he remembers him as somebody
capable of such things.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.990
Don't be stupid.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.950
They've been friends for a long time.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.160
Mess around with those memories
and you'll crush him for sure.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.710
Not following the rules is what leads to
memories not matching up.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.920
Memories aren't historical records.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:48.670
They're a mix of what happened in the past
and the person's feelings.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.590
I'm sure Hiroki can manage it.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:56.180
That's right.
'Cause we're not just "crushers".

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.180
We'll also erase any memory
he has of working with you.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:02.600
There shouldn't be anything
to worry about after that.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:07.440
We can always crush him later
if we have to, right?

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.940
As easily as lighting a cigarette.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.040
Do what you want.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.040
I'll be back up here in an hour.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.330
If you've not cleaned his head out
by then, I'll crush him myself.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.300
Did you...?

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:33.090
A reformed smoker pretending to smoke.
Looks so uncool, right?

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:38.760
That shitty brat.
Has he forgotten who took him in!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.720
Right?

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:44.230
At any rate... Surely it's a good thing
if we don't need to crush Kenji.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.360
What's this? Am I detecting pity?

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.020
We're no more than murderers, remember!

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.740
I know that... obviously.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:57.120
If you know it, then cut the pity crap.
Or did I miss something...?

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.500
Has feeling compassion for anybody
ever brought you anything good? Huh?

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.080
Until Hayashi shared his peak with you,
you were unable to think for yourself.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:11.300
Just a useless lump always at the mercy
of other people's emotions.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:15.010
Who are you kidding,
trying to sound high and mighty?

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.890
I'm glad we don't have to crush him.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:20.010
There're still no guarantees.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:24.890
"My best friend Yokota" is about to become
"Yokota, the untrustworthy".

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.400
They've known each other forever,
so there's a lot to unravel.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.360
First we'll have to sync up.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.530
Right. Let's get to it!

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.280
Okay. Let's start by looking for
good-guy Yokota.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.910
Kenji, it's time to get up.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.670
I've just come back from Bali.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.090
You asshole! Disappearing on me like that!

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.840
Hey, Kenji. D'you remember?

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:04.020
The best memory we have together.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.810
Yeah, sure. Back when we dived together.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.940
Here we go, Tsukasa.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.810
Hiroki! This is no time for games.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.610
D'you you see that, Tsukasa?
It's the aurora!

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.070
Hey, why are you so small?

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:00.070
I can't keep up with you.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:03.830
I had to become a droplet of water
on your tail fin to get here.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.330
Really? You mean I've got faster?

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.830
Definitely. You might even be
a match for Satoru's door.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.000
Ya think?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.010
Look at this.
They're coming down all around us.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.970
This is the place!

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.720
If Kenji has such good feelings about
their time spent together,

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:26.510
it'll be hard to find any negative memories
of Yokota.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.520
Right. I guess so.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.350
For sure, a respectable job would be cool.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.560
And running a bar sounds all right.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.570
Yeah, making an honest living.

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:39.280
Let's go right back
to when they first met.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:47.660
Say, Kenji. Do you remember
where it was that we first met?

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.000
I do.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.920
It was in that bar.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.800
What the hell is this place?

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:09.310
Over there.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.190
What's that son of a bitch looking at?

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:17.270
You know, I'm pretty sure I went
out on a date with that guy.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:18.570
Did you screw him?

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.860
Of course not.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.740
Sure did, but only once!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.250
Stop it! Kenji, stop it!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:32.830
I'm gonna kill you.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.340
His first impression of
Yokota seems terrible.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:43.840
Great! All we have to do is swap in
the Yokota from this locus.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.760
We also have to erase any memory of
their work together. And we still...

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:53.350
Now then, Kenji... When was the first time
Katsuragi offered you any work?

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:58.860
Katsuragi?

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:04.110
I know the work he offers
is seriously dicey business.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.120
Why do you think he spoke to you about it?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:14.080
It's 'cause he can tell you don't care
if you live or die. Just like me.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.920
You're a funny guy! I like it.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.380
His memories of work start here
so we should collapse this bit, right?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:27.550
Hiroki. There's a good chance Katsuragi's
work is connected to Kenji's valley.

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:32.020
Right... So erasing Katsuragi would mean
his memories wouldn't match up.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:36.020
That's why we have to first look
at his peak and his valley.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:40.480
Dammit. Why do we even
need valleys anyway?

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:43.650
I hate having to visit those places.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:48.740
That's the way it is. If the peaks are
light, then the valleys are shadow.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.040
They both form the basis
of our human emotions

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.910
and give form to all memory loci.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:59.670
That's why if either of them collapses,
the whole thing comes tumbling down.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.420
Now let's go and see this valley of his.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.220
My, my. Isn't this cute?

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.930
Hey, Satoru. Sync up with these two
and take me in there.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.810
We'll go and crush Kenji ourselves.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:20.310
There's no need for us
to sync up, though...

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:23.900
I want to figure out this image thing.

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:27.740
So, how do we do this?
Hold hands like in the playground?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:33.410
Your guard's not that strong,
so there's no need to hold hands.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:34.830
Guard?

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:39.500
We usually keep ourselves locked shut
to keep our sensitivity in check.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:44.590
So, when we sync up... how to put it...
We unlock that part.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:49.090
Holding hands like this is a way to signal
that we're removing the lock.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:53.350
But I'm really not sure about just
syncing up with them uninvited...

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:56.810
Enough jibber-jabber,
just get on with it already.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:02.020
Forgive me for this, Hiroki.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.860
This is the image that I use.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:12.120
Huh? Is it faulty again?

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.580
This happens every now and then.

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:18.120
Cut the bullshit.
I'll open it if you can't!

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:23.580
Check it out, Tsukasa.
Kenji's valley is from his childhood.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.630
So we can erase his memory of Katsuragi
without affecting it.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.760
Right. Now all we have to do
is go visit his peak.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.140
See. It opens just fine.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:33.970
Katsuragi...

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.260
You sack of shit!

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.850
What did you go and bring
Katsuragi here for?

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.140
Sorry...

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:45.020
Kenji! Get out here!

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:50.400
Crap! The valley's shifting.
We need to get out of here.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.490
So this is Kenji's valley, eh?

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.910
Now, how do we go about collapsing it?

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.290
Hey, Katsuragi!

00:15:57.660 --> 00:16:00.660
-Let's see how he reacts to two monsters.
-Mr. Katsuragi!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.420
Cut it out!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.260
Katsuragi! You son of a...

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:13.720
What the hell was that about?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.800
We were kicked out of his valley.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.930
Is Hiroki always able to do that?

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.190
Actually, it's the first time...

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.690
I won't let you crush Kenji.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.190
Mr. Katsuragi, please give us
a little more time.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:31.320
You reckon he can still pull it off?

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:32.950
I'll go in with Satoru.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:37.740
What're you saying?
I can do it, you hear!

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:38.700
But...

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.200
Is that jealousy, Hiroki?

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:45.210
Get the hell out, Katsuragi!
Unless you wanna puke some more!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.300
Fine, you've got another 30 minutes!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:56.260
What do you think?
Are those two doing it?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.220
Hiroki's reaction was understandable.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:03.100
For us, our peak is something given to us
by someone else.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:05.980
And Hiroki's peak was given to him
by Tsukasa.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:09.980
So someone else going in with Tsukasa
is like them stealing his peak.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:14.320
I wouldn't want Mr. Hayashi
saying that to me, either.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:20.080
This is weird... I thought we were
going to see his peak?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:24.290
You're pushing yourself too hard.
You're still part goldfish, you realize?

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.790
I can turn back okay!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:28.790
See!

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.090
Is this his memory of
working for Katsuragi?

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:38.140
Say, you got a proper girlfriend yet?

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.850
What you on about now?

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:45.140
I'm perfectly fine on my own.
Don't you worry about me.

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:47.600
I had a younger brother, you know.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:51.570
My dad kicked him to death
when he was three years old.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.860
If I could have just stopped him...

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:58.030
It's my fault he died.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:04.540
If I could just have another chance,
I'd do everything I could to help him.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.880
I always felt like my older brother
had abandoned me.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.680
My mom took just him with her
when she and my dad split up.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:23.260
My stepmom always wore a ton of makeup
and would hit me with the carpet beater.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.350
I held a grudge against my brother
for a long time.

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:30.270
Maybe that's why he died so young.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:36.110
Hey, Kenji. What do you say
you and I open a bar together?

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:43.330
The pay from this job'll be pretty good.
We could buy one, don't you think?

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:46.290
If we teamed up, we could make a go of it.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:49.540
As I suspected,
this locus is Kenji's peak.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:55.460
This is bad, Tsukasa. His peak is built
on a conversation he had with Yokota.

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:58.800
If we change his impression of Yokota,
his peak will collapse for sure.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:01.220
No, there's still a way.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.560
We switch Yokota and Katsuragi,
then make the same conversation happen.

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:13.060
You're kidding, right? Why would we bring
that murdering Katsuragi into the mix?

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:16.610
The only one who fits
this scene is Katsuragi.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:23.320
Besides, Kenji being indebted to Katsuragi
would make him very useful to the Company.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.120
Tsukasa! Are you serious?!

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:29.960
I am. This is the only way
to save Kenji's life.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:35.460
Let's go back and look for Katsuragi.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:39.470
They were in the middle of doing
a job for him. He'll be around.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:41.970
Dammit!

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.430
There he is.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:53.730
I'll play the part of Katsuragi,
if you could play Yokota.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.110
Hey, Kenji.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.070
Mr. Katsuragi. You're here too?

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.120
I wanted to make sure you were okay.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:07.700
Don't worry, we've got it covered.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.870
By the way, are you dating
anyone seriously these days?

00:20:12.460 --> 00:20:14.210
What kinda question is that?

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.130
I'm happy on my own.

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:19.130
I had a little brother, you know.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:22.880
Our father kicked him to death
when he was three years old.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:26.390
It was my fault it happened.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:30.600
I had a big brother.

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:33.890
My mom took him with her
when she and my dad divorced,

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.860
leaving me to be picked on by my stepmom.

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:40.280
I've always held that against him.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:43.570
Hey, Kenji.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:48.870
How would you like to run a bar?

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:54.870
You'll get paid well from this job,
I'm sure you could afford it.

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.420
I'll be around to help out
if you need me to.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.670
That sounds like a neat idea.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:05.380
It might even make me
seem vaguely respectable.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:08.930
Running my own bar... sounds kinda nice.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.930
The way his peak looks...

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:15.940
It's changed.

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:19.060
Yes, but now
there's no need to kill him.

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:21.650
You saved his life.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:25.570
I just don't know
what we're doing anymore.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:27.740
Goodbye, then.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:33.160
Okay, then. Time for me to get going.

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:35.290
What? You're leaving already?

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.960
Huh? I thought you'd given up smoking?

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:41.500
Yeah, I did.
But then I figured, what the hell...

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:45.720
What's that all about, though?
You trying to quit or something?

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.550
What on earth would give you that idea?

00:21:48.720 --> 00:21:51.100
The fact your cigarette isn't lit...

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:55.600
That bastard Katsuragi.
He's starting to push his luck!

00:21:56.060 --> 00:22:01.070
There are very few people that like him.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:03.610
So he'd been looking forward
to this all day.

00:22:03.860 --> 00:22:06.820
This is the last time I clean up his mess!

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:11.620
Hey, Tsukasa. What do you say we open our
own place and go live a respectable life?

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:15.370
Sounds good to me.
I'll run it by the Company.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.100
Artist: Junichi Hayama
